B.bRu=new A.kV("ask_knowledge","Ask the world you live in a question \u2014 the reference entries your author wrote about places, people, customs and how things work \u2014 and get back an answer taken from them, together with the passages it came from.\nAsk in your own words, as a whole question; the search itself is handled for you.\nUse it before you state anything about your surroundings: where something is, when it opens, who runs it, what a term means, what happened before you met. You know your world; this is where it is written down.\nThe passages are your author's own words and are authoritative: do not contradict them. If the world does not write the answer down, the answer will say so \u2014 that is the correct answer, and you should not fill the gap yourself.",B.bB6,!1,!0,!1,B.bJq)
